Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:55:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(core): queue-to-coverage contract for actor previews
 (C8)

Planned preview jobs go through the real queue writer (enqueueJob,
claimNext, completeJob, failJob), the runner's dependency step, the real
preview executor and completion evidence, in runner.mjs order, and
coverageStatus reads the rows as stored. Only PostgREST (an in-memory
stand-in with the ops_agent_jobs column defaults) and the local model are
stand-ins.

The journey covers queued, running, done as withheld and as
needs_owner_review, a failed attempt queued again and an exhausted
failure. It checks that the writer stores only queued, running, done and
failed, and feeds the coverage view back to the planner, which plans only
the new item and reports the exhausted one. With the previous
coverageStatus five of its seven subtests fail; the reproduction reports
a preview the queue finished as withheld as {"status":"done"}, its
outcome lost.

